{# The public page of a shared communication (issue #706, IT-04) —
   Controller\PublicPageController::show().

   What Facebook, WhatsApp and Messenger read to build the preview of a
   link somebody posted, and what a human following that link lands on.

   **It carries exactly what was published**: the card the browser drew,
   the title and the text the first destination received. Never the album
   the communication came from, never its other photos, never an
   article's body — the album stays « Membres connectés », and sharing
   one of its photos in a card is not a decision to publish the album.
   Anything added here is added to what an anonymous visitor may read, so
   add nothing without revisiting SECURITY.md § 6. #}
{% extends "base.html.twig" %}

{% block title %}{{ title }} — {{ site_name }}{% endblock %}

{% block head_meta %}
    {# Never indexed, and that is not a contradiction with the Open Graph
       tags below: a link preview renders an address somebody chose to
       post, which is a different act from offering it to every search.
       The address is the authorisation here, and a search result would
       hand it to people nobody shared it with. The news module's own
       shareable preview says the same (views/preview.html.twig). #}
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex">

    <meta property="og:type" content="article">
    <meta property="og:title" content="{{ title }}">
    {% if body %}<meta property="og:description" content="{{ body }}">{% endif %}
    {% if og_url %}<meta property="og:url" content="{{ og_url }}">{% endif %}
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ site_name }}">
    {% if og_image_url %}
        <meta property="og:image" content="{{ og_image_url }}">
        <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
    {% else %}
        <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">
    {% endif %}
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ title }}">
    {% if body %}<meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ body }}">{% endif %}
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-12 col-lg-8">
            <h1 class="h3 mb-4">{{ title }}</h1>

            {% if og_image_url %}
                <img src="{{ og_image_url }}" alt="" class="rounded mb-4 w-100" decoding="async">
            {% endif %}

            {% if body %}
                <p class="mb-4">{{ body|nl2br }}</p>
            {% endif %}

            {% if source_path %}
                {# Gone the day the album or the article is deleted, and
                   the page then shows what was published with no button.
                   Where it leads applies its own rule to whoever follows
                   it: an album is « Membres connectés », so a visitor
                   with no account is asked to sign in — which is the
                   point, not an oversight. #}
                <a href="{{ source_path }}" class="btn btn-primary">Voir sur le site</a>
            {% endif %}
        </div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
